\f0\fs24 \cf2 <$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 \'93Hey!\'94 the Candid Criminal production manager called. \'93Careful with those!\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Two stagehands were loading a nativity scene into a truck and bashed Joseph\'92s head on the door. The production manager wondered whether the set designer hadn\'92t slipped the crew a few shekels to destroy the whole ensemble of figures. The Three Wise Men looked like Alexander with different beards, Joseph looked like their clean-shaven father and Baby Jesus looked like a shaved koala with his beady Alexander eyes, blunt Alexander nose, and rounded Alexander ears.\
As for Mary, the production manager could not even form the syllables of the name of the person Mary looked like. The blonde hair alone was borderline blasphemy. Since when was the Blessed Mother a Viking? And since when did she have calves like that?\
Last to load were water tanks and the fibreglass containers that looked like rounded oversized coffins for boating enthusiasts.\
Alexander watched the truck doors shut, the drivers climb in, and the trucks roll out of the studio\'92s loading yard.\
\'93Who\'92d have thought it would take so many trucks?\'94 he muttered to himself.\
The rest of the crew climbed into a bus. Against advice, Alexander chose to save himself a good couple of hours and travel up to Sublime Point by hover-copt. What was the point of having a hover pad at his mountain home if he didn\'92t use it? His PA had explained that his life insurance would not cover the trip, so Alexander pulled a few strings and borrowed one of his mother\'92s Shakti Enterprises hover-copts. That seemed to settle the whole kerfuffle down.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Alexander never made it to the hover pad.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 The UDF checkpoint refused the Candid Criminal convoy entry, on the basis that they needed to turn 
\f2\i someone
\f1\i0  back after the Elvi invasion. Apparently having Alexander\'92s face, 
\fs20 CANDID CRIMINAL
\fs22  and 
\fs20 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 YOU COULD BE NEXT
\fs22  painted on all the sides of all the trucks constituted no right of passage into the \'93conflict zone.\'94\
Alexander had his hover-copt land in the middle of the highway, blocking traffic both ways. He jumped from the cabin, straightened his tie and sauntered towards the checkpoint rolling his shoulders, one after the other as he went. He imagined how good he looked in an action scene and tripped over his toes.\
As he approached, he studied the UDF personnel at the checkpoint. If there was one thing Alexander was good at, it was spotting a fan, and he spotted a couple among the dills in uniform. He locked eyes with one of them and continued to saunter\'97he even slowed down a little to hold the tension.\
\'93Is there a reason you are preventing me from going home for Christmas?\'94 he asked one of the fans.\
\'93Sir, no sir!\'94 the lieutenant answered.\
Another officer stepped forward to meet Alexander\'97not a fan. \'93What\'92s in the truck?\'94\
Another officer stepped back to talk on her radio\'97also not a fan.\
\'93Christmas presents,\'94 Alexander said and made his face do his television smile.\
\'93For the whole village?\'94 Not-a-Fan challenged.\
\'93Well, yes,\'94 Alexander answered and winked. \'93And the whole country, as a matter of fact.\'94\
Fan\'92s face lit up; she guessed and blurted, \'93You\'92re recording a Candid Criminal episode!\'94\
\'93Even better. I\'92m broadcasting a Christmas special, live from my compound.\'94\
\'93That\'92s amazing!\'94\
\'93Isn\'92t it?\'94\
\'93I hear the Wheel of Death is rigged,\'94 Not-a-Fan said. \'93You already know how the guilty gets executed.\'94\
Alexander stood back at an angle. \'93Well, I can neither confirm nor deny\'85 production secrets, all that stuff.\'94\
Fan looked up and down the truck convoy. \'93Come on, you can tell us. We can keep a secret.\'94\
Alexander made a performance of acquiescing, as if for an old friend. He leaned in and whispered, \'93Shark tank.\'94\
Fan\'92s eyes bulged with surprise.\
\'93Come on,\'94 Not-a-Fan said while she adjusted the rifle on her shoulder. \'93Where are you getting the sharks?\'94\
\'93Brought them with us,\'94 Alexander answered.\
\'93Bull tax!\'94 Not-a-Fan accused.\
Alexander pointed to the next-to-last truck. \'93They\'92re in there.\'94\
\'93That\'92s not enough room to swim in. Everyone knows sharks need to swim to keep breathing.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Alexander looked at Not-a-Fan. \'93Well that is true for obligate ram ventilators like the great white and the mako, but other species like the tiger and the bull shark have incredibly strong cheek and throat muscles to pull water over their gills.\'94\
Not-a-Fan blinked. \'93Well, okay then. Which ones have you got? Tiger sharks?\'94\
\'93Oh, no,\'94 Alexander chortled and waved the remark down. \'93Bull sharks have the strongest bite kilo-for-kilo. They\'92re smaller and nastier, perfect for a travelling road show.\'94\
\'93Wow!\'94 Fan said. \'93I did not know that.\'94\
\'93Which truck is the prisoner in?\'94 Not-a-Fan asked with a little more interest. \'93Or are you planning on arresting a billionaire in their pyjamas.\'94\
Alexander decided to play the mystery. \'93Um, the second one.\'94\
Fan gasped.\
\'93So, tell me why you good folks are here? Gas leak? Cosplay festival?\'94 Alexander asked, looking back at the queue of cars snaking back behind his convoy.\
Fan squealed. \'93It\'92s your mother, isn\'92t it?\'94\
\'93What?\'94 Alexander asked, stunned.\
\'93It all makes sense now! We\'92re here to shut her down.\'94\
Alexander masked his shock and tapped his nose. \'93You\'92ll have to watch the show.\'94\
Fan called up the chain of command on her radio. Within the time of a toilet paper ad, orders came back.\
\'93Let them pass.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Alexander sent the hover-copt back to the city and rode shotgun in the lead truck. They\'92d only negotiated the bridge, the roundabout and were halfway down the mall when he observed, \'93There are a lot of Elvi in town.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 Elvi had filled caf\'e9 outdoor areas and were gorging on multi-course breakfasts. Guitar cases leaned against tables. One was carrying a small amplifier out of a shop that normally sold lamps. Buskers performed outside every third shopfront window. On the corner a group of skateboard kids were arguing over who had discovered rock and roll. Though Alexander couldn\'92t hear the conversation, one of the kids said, \'93Doesn\'92t matter who invented it, my dad owns it,\'94 and went on to explain that music was just an undeveloped resource that had no intrinsic value until an agent or manager or publishing house came along and figured out how to sell it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0
\cf2 The convoy passed through the village and turned down Sublime Point Road. If Alexander was only mildly surprised by the number of Elvi buskers, he was not prepared for the number of tents lining both sides of the road wherever there had been a vacant space. Alexander was even more perplexed by the campers being Elvi. As far as he could see, they were camping under trees on the golf course too. The trucks slowed to pass Cadillacs and coffee carts being rolled down the middle of the street.\
At another checkpoint a lieutenant recognised Alexander and asked him to sign the sleeve of his fatigues for his mother.\
\'93For your mother? Of course. Make sure she watches tonight.\'94 Alexander was in his element.\
\'93She\'92s dead, sir, choked on a cocktail frankfurt at the end of a helium chamber episode.\'94\
The convoy rolled onto a section of road that passed through the golf course. Greens and bunkers appeared out of the tree rough on both sides. Through the trees, Alexander saw tents in the rough. He saw an Elvine receiving instruction from a small boy who demonstrated club grip, stance and swinging, then stepped aside while the Elvine sliced the ball into a tree. Both seemed pleased.\
Alexander nearly jumped out of his underwear, startled by the sound of gunfire in his ear. The truck\'92s windscreen cracked.\
\'93We\'92re under fire!\'94 the driver called and leapt from the cabin.\
Alexander fell out of the truck in terror. He fell heavily, but rolled and crouched close by a tyre. Artillery continued to bombard the roof and the truck\'92s sides.\
\'93Sorry!\'94 someone called out with a very familiar voice.\
\'93Yeah, we\'92re still learning this game,\'94 said the same voice from a slightly different position on the wind.\
Alexander found the courage to straighten and look over the truck\'92s bonnet. Four Elvi were walking off a golf fairway towards the convoy.\
\'93We got caught in a sand trap,\'94 an Elvi explained.\
\'93Yeah, and we couldn\'92t chip out,\'94 another said.\
A third flipped the two-wood he was holding and sang into its fat end, \'93Because we love golf too much baby.\'94\
\'93Hey, that\'92s pretty good,\'94 said a fourth. \'93Who needs the Great Teacher anyway?\'94\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl220\sb220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 <!$Scr_Ps::1><$Scr_Ps::0>
\f1\fs22 Near the compound, the roadside crowd thickened. Elvi looked up from camp chairs as the trucks passed. A few applauded. Alexander raised a hand, then discovered they were applauding an Elvis who had climbed onto the roof of a limousine with a guitar.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs24 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
<!$Scr_Ps::0><$Scr_Ps::1>
\f1\fs22 The road curved left and Alexander saw the compound gates. He leaned forward to where he knew the cameras would be watching; the gates opened. Two Shakti drones dropped into view and escorted the convoy.\
By the time they reached the auditorium carpark, the aquarium attendant was requesting shade and the riggers were requesting clear access. The bus emptied.\
Eloise stood outside the auditorium like she was guarding the door. \
Alexander jumped from the truck. \'93Mother!\'94 He hailed.\
\'93Alexander.\'94 Eloise waited for Alexander to cross the carpark to her. She looked along the convoy.\
\'93I heard you had abandoned your post in Liechtenstein. I swear, Heinrich sounded like he expected to be executed.\'94\
\'93He should know, I\'92m the one that hands out executions,\'94 Alexander said, sounding miffed.\
\'93Show business executions. Your scripts don\'92t make it real.\'94\
\'93You should try telling a Hollywood producer that,\'94 Alexander countered.\
\'93Have you noticed the UDF seem to want to pick a fight with me?\'94\
\'93The place is teeming with Elvi too. They tried to kill me with golf balls.\'94\
\'93Exactly. Try not to get caught in the crossfire, dear.\'94
